---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Header from '../../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../../components/Footer.astro';
import Giscus from '../../components/Giscus.astro';

const lang = 'en' as const;
---

<Layout
  title="Workspace & Organization in SoloMD — File Tree Sorting, Outline, Search, Backlinks, Bases & Mobile"
  description="Organize a folder of Markdown notes in SoloMD: custom-sortable file tree, outline navigation, workspace search, tags, backlinks, Bases properties table, saved views, daily notes, and iOS/Android workspaces."
  lang={lang}
>
  <Header lang={lang} />
  <main id="main">
    <article class="container docs-article">
      <nav class="breadcrumbs">
        <a href="/">Home</a> / <a href="/docs/">Docs</a> / <span>Workspace</span>
      </nav>

      <h1>Workspace &amp; Organization</h1>
      <p class="lead">Open a folder once; the file tree, outline, backlinks, properties table, and full-text search work on top of it immediately.</p>

      <h2>1. File tree (sorting, drag-and-drop, context actions)</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Toggle</strong>: press <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + B</kbd> (or click the sidebar button in the header on macOS, Windows, and Linux).</li>
        <li><strong>Four sorting modes</strong>: sort by <strong>Name</strong>, <strong>Creation Date</strong>, <strong>Modification Date</strong>, or <strong>drag files into your own custom manual order</strong> (new files go to the end).</li>
        <li><strong>Inline creation &amp; keyboard shortcuts</strong>: create notes (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + Shift + N</kbd>) or folders right inside the selected folder; press <kbd>F2</kbd> to rename and <kbd>Del</kbd> to move to the system Trash (with confirmation); right-click to <strong>Expand / Collapse All Subfolders</strong> or <strong>Copy Relative Path</strong>.</li>
        <li><strong>Visual indicators</strong>: open files show an indicator dot; optionally enable <strong>Folder item count badges</strong> and <strong>Double-click to open files</strong>; image attachment folders (<code>_assets</code>, <code>*.assets</code>) stay hidden unless “Show hidden files” is turned on; switching tabs automatically reveals and highlights the active file in the tree (configurable).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>2. Outline &amp; keyboard jump labels</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Toggle with <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Shift + O</kbd>. Click any heading to jump accurately in Live Edit, Split, or Preview, and collapse sections.</li>
        <li><strong>Jump labels</strong>: press the letter shown next to a heading to jump from the keyboard, or press <code>g</code> + line number to jump to a line.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>3. Right-sidebar panes</h2>
      <p>
        Right-click the sidebar (or use the command palette) to toggle panes; drag to reorder and resize. Hide the whole strip with <kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + B</kbd>.
      </p>
      <table class="kb-table">
        <thead><tr><th>Pane</th><th>What it shows</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><th>Search (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘+Shift+F</kbd>)</th><td>Ripgrep-fast full-text search across the workspace folder (case, whole word, regex).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Backlinks</th><td>Every note linking to the current one via <code>[[note]]</code>, <code>[[folder/note]]</code>, or <code>[[note.md]]</code> (ignoring code fences).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Relationships &amp; Neighborhood</th><td>Typed forward + inverse links from front-matter and an interactive neighborhood graph explorer.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Tags</th><td>All <code>#tags</code> in the workspace (including CJK tags, while ignoring hex color codes like <code>#fff</code> in tables and code).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>History</th><td>Local Git snapshot timeline per note with one-click diff and rollback (see <a href="/docs/sync/">Sync &amp; History</a>).</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Properties</th><td>Visual form inspector for YAML front-matter properties.</td></tr>
          <tr><th>Agent</th><td>Chat with your vault (see <a href="/docs/ai/">AI features</a>).</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>

      <h2>4. Bases &amp; Saved Views</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Bases (your notes as a table)</strong>: Command palette → “Workspace: Properties Table (Bases)” opens every note as a row in a sortable, filterable table built from front-matter properties.</li>
        <li><strong>Saved views</strong>: persistent filtered note lists stored as <code>.solomd/views/*.yml</code> in the workspace, listed under the file tree.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>5. Daily notes, Quick Capture &amp; Inbox</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Daily notes (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + D</kbd>)</strong>: opens today’s daily note on demand; yesterday and tomorrow are one command away.</li>
        <li><strong>Quick Capture (<kbd>Ctrl/⌘ + Alt + Shift + M</kbd>) &amp; Inbox</strong>: capture thoughts from anywhere or from the Web Clipper browser extension, and triage them with “Mark Organized &amp; Advance”.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>6. iPhone, iPad &amp; Android Workspaces</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>iPhone &amp; iPad</strong>: pick any folder in the Files app (iCloud Drive, On My iPhone, or third-party cloud providers) as your persistent workspace; notes opened from the Files app are edited in place; long-press or tap <code>⋯</code> in the file tree to rename, move, or delete.</li>
        <li><strong>Android</strong>: create folders in the file tree, open Daily Notes, paste/insert images into <code>_assets/</code>, and automatically reload externally synced notes (e.g. Syncthing) inside Android SAF vaults.</li>
      </ul>

      <Giscus />
    </article>
  </main>
  <Footer lang={lang} />
</Layout>
